{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"d054000000009001","type":"group","x":0,"y":340,"width":1600,"height":1110,"label":"01 · 发展与生产资源 / Development and resources","color":"5"},
		{"id":"d054000000009002","type":"group","x":1800,"y":340,"width":1600,"height":1110,"label":"02 · 价格与分类 / Prices and classifications","color":"5"},
		{"id":"d054000000009003","type":"group","x":0,"y":1770,"width":1600,"height":1690,"label":"03 · 贫困识别与深度 / Identifying and measuring poverty","color":"4"},
		{"id":"d054000000009004","type":"group","x":1800,"y":1770,"width":1600,"height":1690,"label":"04 · 完整分布 / The full distribution","color":"2"},
		{"id":"d054000000009005","type":"group","x":0,"y":3780,"width":1600,"height":1210,"label":"05 · 平均成就与联合剥夺 / Achievements and joint deprivation","color":"6"},
		{"id":"d054000000009006","type":"group","x":1800,"y":3780,"width":1600,"height":1210,"label":"06 · 增长与贯通应用 / Growth and integrated comparisons","color":"3"},
		{"id":"d054000000003000","type":"text","x":0,"y":0,"width":3400,"height":240,"text":"# 发展、贫困与不平等的测量\n\n连续阅读：[[02_Economy/10_发展经济学/07_发展水平、贫困与分配|发展水平、贫困与分配]]。按区号从左到右、从上到下阅读；卡片标题打开共享原子，短桥说明跨区关系。颜色只区分问题，不表示掌握程度。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nRead the [[02_Economy/10_发展经济学/07_发展水平、贫困与分配|continuous course chapter]], or follow the numbered sections from left to right and top to bottom. Card titles open shared atoms; bridge cards explain cross-section relationships. Colors distinguish questions, not mastery.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000001","type":"text","x":60,"y":430,"width":400,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### [[经济发展]]\n\n生产与社会结构的改善，要接到健康、教育和生活机会等结果上。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Economic development*\n\nImprovements in production and social organization must connect to health, education and opportunities in people's lives.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000001001","type":"text","x":600,"y":430,"width":400,"height":350,"text":"### [[国内生产总值|GDP]]\n\n一定时期的生产流量；增加值汇总避免中间品重复计算。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Gross domestic product*\n\nA flow of production during a period; value-added accounting avoids double-counting intermediate goods.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000003","type":"text","x":1140,"y":430,"width":400,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### [[人均GDP]]\n\nGDP 除以同期人口，表示平均产出，不是每人实际领到的收入。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*GDP per capita*\n\nGDP divided by the corresponding population measures average production, not income actually received by each person.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000008","type":"text","x":60,"y":990,"width":400,"height":350,"text":"### [[GDP与福利]]\n\n生产流量、财富存量和生活福利是不同对象；GDP 也并非只记市场交易。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*GDP and welfare*\n\nProduction flows, wealth stocks and well-being are distinct. GDP is not restricted to market transactions.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000001002","type":"text","x":600,"y":990,"width":400,"height":350,"text":"### [[实际GDP增长]]\n\n用可比价格或链式数量口径识别产出量变化，分开涨价与增产。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Real GDP growth*\n\nComparable prices or chain-volume measures distinguish increased production from higher prices.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000004","type":"text","x":1140,"y":990,"width":400,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### [[国民总收入|GNI · 国民总收入]]\n\nGDP 加跨境净初次收入，转向常住单位的收入归属；常住不等于国籍。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Gross national income*\n\nAdding net primary income from abroad shifts from domestic production to income accruing to residents. Residence is not citizenship.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000005","type":"text","x":1860,"y":430,"width":400,"height":350,"color":"5","text":"### [[购买力平价|PPP · 购买力平价]]\n\n跨经济体的统计价格转换率；GDP 与消费要匹配各自的 PPP。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Purchasing power parity*\n\nA statistical price conversion across economies. Match the PPP to GDP, consumption or the relevant aggregate.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000006","type":"text","x":2400,"y":430,"width":400,"height":350,"text":"### [[汇率与购买力比较]]\n\n外币结算看适用汇率，实际量比较看对应 PPP；先确定问题再换算。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Choosing the conversion*\n\nUse the applicable exchange rate for foreign-currency settlement and the corresponding PPP for volume comparisons. Choose the question first.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000007","type":"text","x":2940,"y":430,"width":400,"height":350,"text":"### [[收入分组与发展分类]]\n\n世界银行收入组、UNDP 的 HDI 等级与 IMF 分组各有标准和版本。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Income and development groups*\n\nWorld Bank income groups, UNDP HDI categories and IMF groups use distinct criteria and editions.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000003001","type":"text","x":1860,"y":990,"width":1480,"height":350,"text":"### 同一收入概念，两条转换路径\n\n[[国民总收入|人均 GNI]]经 Atlas 法换算，进入[[收入分组与发展分类|世界银行收入分组]]；按相应 [[购买力平价|PPP]] 换算，则进入[[人类发展指数|HDI 的收入维度]]。同一个国家可以同时拥有不同体系的标签，不能互相替代。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nAtlas-method GNI per capita feeds World Bank income groups. PPP GNI per capita feeds the HDI income dimension. The same income concept enters different conversions and classifications; one label cannot replace another.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000024","type":"text","x":60,"y":1870,"width":400,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[贫困测量的福利口径]]\n\n先定收入或消费内容、家庭到个人的换算、人口权重，以及价格和期间。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Welfare-measure conventions*\n\nSpecify income or consumption, household-to-person conversion, population weights, prices and periods before measuring poverty.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000020","type":"text","x":600,"y":1870,"width":400,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[贫困线]]\n\n指定福利变量的识别阈值；货币例采用 $y<z$，金额单位、期间和价格须匹配。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Poverty line*\n\nA threshold for a specified welfare measure. Monetary examples use $y<z$, with matching units, periods and prices.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000021","type":"text","x":1140,"y":1870,"width":400,"height":350,"text":"### [[绝对贫困与相对贫困]]\n\n绝对线固定实际生活标准；相对线依社会分布变化。固定实际不等于冻结名义金额。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Absolute and relative poverty*\n\nAn absolute line fixes a real living standard; a relative line depends on the distribution. A fixed real line need not be fixed in nominal terms.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000022","type":"text","x":60,"y":2440,"width":400,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[贫困人口比例|H · 贫困人口比例]]\n\n贫困人数除以总人口。没有人越线时，线下增收不会改变 H。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Headcount ratio*\n\nPoor people divided by the whole population. Income gains below the line leave H unchanged if nobody crosses it.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000023","type":"text","x":600,"y":2440,"width":400,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[贫困缺口指数|PG · 贫困缺口指数]]\n\n每人的标准化短缺对全体人口平均；非贫困者缺口为零，仍在分母中。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Poverty gap index*\n\nAverage normalized shortfalls over everyone. Nonpoor people contribute zero gaps but remain in the denominator.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000025","type":"text","x":1140,"y":2440,"width":400,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[贫困者平均缺口|IGR · 贫困者平均缺口]]\n\n只对贫困人口平均。有人贫困时 $PG=H\\,IGR$；无人贫困时 IGR 未定义。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Income gap ratio*\n\nAverage only among poor people. When poverty exists, $PG=H\\,IGR$. IGR is undefined when nobody is poor.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000026","type":"text","x":600,"y":3020,"width":400,"height":350,"color":"4","text":"### [[平方贫困缺口|P₂ · 平方贫困缺口]]\n\n先平方个人缺口，再对全人口平均；可区分同 H、同 PG 的贫困者内部差异。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Squared poverty gap*\n\nSquare individual gaps before averaging over everyone. P₂ can distinguish within-poor distributions with equal H and PG.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000040","type":"text","x":1860,"y":1870,"width":400,"height":350,"color":"2","text":"### [[洛伦兹曲线]]\n\n收入非负且总额为正时，从低到高排序，描画累计人口与累计收入份额；不显示绝对水平。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Lorenz curve*\n\nFor nonnegative incomes with a positive total, order incomes and plot cumulative population and income shares. The curve does not reveal absolute levels.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000041","type":"text","x":2940,"y":1870,"width":400,"height":350,"color":"2","text":"### [[基尼系数]]\n\n在非负收入、正均值口径下概括全分布相对差距；等于洛伦兹曲线与平等线间面积的两倍。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Gini coefficient*\n\nWith nonnegative incomes and a positive mean, it summarizes relative inequality: twice the area between the Lorenz curve and equality.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000043","type":"text","x":1860,"y":2440,"width":400,"height":350,"text":"### [[相同基尼与分布形状]]\n\n同均值、同基尼，仍可有不同底部份额和相交曲线；一个数不能还原完整分布。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Equal Ginis, different shapes*\n\nEqual means and Ginis can coexist with different lower-group shares and crossing curves. One number cannot recover the distribution.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000042","type":"text","x":2940,"y":2440,"width":400,"height":410,"text":"### [[基尼与转移位置]]\n\n等权、非负收入与正均值下，固定人数、均值和排序，等额渐进转移的基尼降幅随排名距离增大。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Rank distance and transfers*\n\nFor equally weighted, nonnegative incomes with a positive mean, hold population size, mean and ranks fixed. Equal progressive transfers reduce the Gini more across longer rank distances.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000003002","type":"text","x":1860,"y":3020,"width":1480,"height":350,"text":"### 同一份家庭分布，两个问题\n\n[[贫困人口比例|H]]、[[贫困缺口指数|PG]] 和[[平方贫困缺口|P₂]]围绕给定贫困线的短缺；[[洛伦兹曲线]]和[[基尼系数]]比较完整分布的相对差距，线以上的人也参与。四人 40、90、120、150 在 $z=100$ 时，可以同时有 $H=0.5$、$PG=0.175$、$G=0.225$。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nH, PG and P₂ measure shortfalls relative to a specified poverty line. Lorenz curves and the Gini describe relative differences across the full distribution, including people above the line. For incomes 40, 90, 120 and 150 with $z=100$, $H=0.5$, $PG=0.175$ and $G=0.225$ answer distinct questions.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000044","type":"text","x":60,"y":3880,"width":400,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### [[人类发展指数|HDI · 人类发展指数]]\n\n健康、教育和 PPP 人均 GNI 的三维标准化指数取几何平均，概括平均成就。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Human Development Index*\n\nThe geometric mean of three normalized dimension indices—health, education and PPP GNI per capita—summarizes average achievement.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000045","type":"text","x":600,"y":3880,"width":400,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### [[多维贫困]]\n\n用明确维度、剥夺门槛和合成规则，联合识别生活不足；需要知道不足落在谁身上。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Multidimensional poverty*\n\nExplicit dimensions, deprivation cutoffs and combining rules jointly identify shortfalls. We need to know who experiences them together.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000046","type":"text","x":1140,"y":3880,"width":400,"height":350,"color":"6","text":"### [[全球多维贫困指数|Global MPI · 全球多维贫困指数]]\n\n2025 十指标方案：家庭分数 $s\\ge1/3$ 识别，再按人数加总。$MPI=H\\,A$，A 只对贫困者平均剥夺。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nThe 2025 ten-indicator system identifies households at $s\\ge1/3$, then aggregates over members. $MPI=H\\,A$; A is mean deprivation intensity among poor people.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000003003","type":"text","x":60,"y":4430,"width":1480,"height":350,"text":"### 平均成就不能识别联合剥夺\n\n[[人类发展指数|HDI]] 的国家平均值，不能告诉我们缺教育、缺健康和缺生活设施的是否同一群人。[[多维贫困]]需要联合分布；[[全球多维贫困指数|全球 MPI]]使用同源家庭调查，不是 $1-HDI$，也不能由不同年份的全国均值拼出来。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nNational averages in the HDI cannot identify whether the same people experience educational, health and living-standard deprivations. Multidimensional analysis needs joint information. The global MPI uses a common household survey; it is neither $1-HDI$ nor a combination of national averages from different years.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000000002","type":"text","x":1860,"y":3880,"width":400,"height":350,"text":"### [[增长与减贫]]\n\n固定人口、实际价格和绝对线时，家庭福利均值增长仍不足以保证 H 下降；还要看分配。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n*Growth and poverty reduction*\n\nWith population, real prices and the absolute line fixed, growth in mean household welfare does not guarantee a lower H. Distribution also matters.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000003004","type":"text","x":2400,"y":3880,"width":940,"height":350,"text":"### 把六个指标算在同一份数据上\n\n从 40、90、120、150 出发，只把 90 提高到 100。计算均值、H、PG、IGR、P₂ 与 G，再解释为什么 IGR 上升不等于有人变穷。\n\n[[02_Economy/10_发展经济学/07_发展水平、贫困与分配#自己完成一次解释|打开课程练习与折叠答案]]\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nStart from 40, 90, 120 and 150, then raise only 90 to 100. Calculate the mean, H, PG, IGR, P₂ and G. Explain why rising IGR does not mean anyone became poorer.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"d054000000003005","type":"text","x":1860,"y":4430,"width":1480,"height":350,"text":"### 回到国别表：先问证据够不够\n\n人均 GDP、基尼与 HDI 可以给出不同排序。没有同口径家庭福利与共同贫困线，不能倒推出货币贫困率；没有同源联合剥夺记录，也算不出全球 MPI。年份、单位和版本必须逐列核对。\n\n[[02_Economy/10_发展经济学/07_发展水平、贫困与分配#6. 用两次比较把这一章连起来|回到课堂国别表的解释]]\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nGDP per capita, Gini and HDI can rank countries differently. Monetary poverty needs comparable household welfare and a common line; the global MPI needs joint deprivation records. Check years, units and versions column by column before making a comparison.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"}
	],
